jobs.description:
What will you do?

As a Warehouse Employee, you and your colleagues make sure that thousands of products find their way through the warehouse every day. You will work in different parts of the logistics process, which means you won't be doing the same task all day.

You can expect to:

- Collect orders using a handheld scanner;
- Check products and make sure orders are complete;
- Process newly arrived goods;
- Pack products safely and correctly;
- Prepare completed orders for transport;
- Work with modern and automated warehouse systems;
- Keep your workplace clean, organised and safe.

Experience in logistics is useful, but your motivation and willingness to learn are just as important.

Working in 3 shifts

This is not a standard 9-to-5 job. You will rotate between morning, afternoon and night shifts. In return, you receive attractive allowances on top of your salary.

Your working hours are:

- 06:00 – 14:45 | Morning shift;
- 14:45 – 23:15 | 25% extra from 20:00;
- 21:15 – 06:00 | 25% extra until midnight and 40% extra between 00:00 and 06:00.

Do you work on Saturday as your sixth working day? You receive a 50% allowance. For Sunday hours, the allowance is 100%.

For this position, it is important that you are comfortable working different shifts. In addition:

- You speak and understand English;
- Full-time availability is required;
- You are looking for a stable job for the long term;
- You live in the Zevenaar, Arnhem or Duiven area;
- You have your own transport. Due to the working hours, public transport is not a suitable option.

Looking for a hands-on role in a clean and high-tech working environment? We need you!

What are you going to do?
As a Production Employee R4R, you play an important role in ensuring that packaging materials meet the required quality standards before being reused or shipped to customers.

Your responsibilities include:

- Cleaning and refurbishing packaging materials;
- Inspecting products for damage and quality issues;
- Sorting and processing materials according to work instructions;
- Performing basic administrative tasks and registrations;
- Reporting deviations and quality concerns;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace;
- Working closely with colleagues from production and logistics departments.

What do we offer?
- A full-time position in day shift;
- €16,17 gross per hour;
- Travel allowance;
- Opportunities for personal growth and development;
- A stable position within a growing international company;
- A pleasant working environment with supportive colleagues;
- Possibility of a permanent contract after a successful period.

Where will you work?
The company is a leading provider of high-quality packaging solutions for the high-tech industry. The company specializes in the production, cleaning, management, and logistics of industrial packaging materials for customers around the world. Innovation, quality, and customer satisfaction are at the heart of everything they do.

What do we ask?
- You are available full-time in day shift;
- You have a good command of English;
- You work accurately and have an eye for detail;
- You are physically fit and enjoy hands-on work;
- Experience in production, logistics, or assembly is a plus, but not required;
- You can work independently as well as in a team;
- You have a positive attitude and are eager to lear

Are you interested?
Are you ready for a new challenge as a Production Employee R4R ?

